  drafted and Gardner Minshew is a you  know a mid round draft pick here  yeah well it's because of why you get  drafted in the mid rounds it's because  you have some type of flaw in your game  that we saw in college whether it be  your decision making your arm strength  your accuracy whatever it is going  through that draft process they've  identified a flaw and so you have to  overcome that and prove that you can do  it at the NFL level because of whatever  that flaw is whereas  when you're a top pick you have some  type of talent where teams are looking  at saying wow  Patrick mahomes look at this arm this is  generational so we're ready to anoint  him because in our minds we are already  pre conceived to be able to see that he  could be great so it's just a matter of  overcoming some preconceived notions  that we have as fans as coaches as  evaluators in the NFL yeah I guess I got  sidetracked because I think Russell  Wilson's been doing this it's just taken  people longer to realize that he's been  doing this I I think he's been as  valuable to his team as anybody any  player in the last couple years so  you've got a chance see him up close and  personal yeah what did you see last  without it because being in Seattle for  whatever reason just because it's such  an East Coast dominant sport in football  and in sports in general Seattle they're  always playing the afternoon game  they're not on everybody's TV as much so  people don't realize how much Russell  Wilson does for this team because he's  not always the guy that's putting up 400  yards but he's always finding a way to  win and that's to me why he's the most  valuable he makes everybody around him  better and he finds a way to win he's  Joe Thomas former Cleveland Browns  all-pro tackle what did you see last  night and as far as what kind of  solutions would you have for the inept  officiating that we've seen inconsistent  officiating we've seen well I think  truthfully we need to eliminate instant  replay because right now the NFL is  selling this folly to its fans that we  have in Surrey play because we want to  get it right and we have all these  different camera angles in these games  and we can clearly see that calls are  not being made correctly and then we go  to instant replay and in our minds we've  been told by the NFL they're doing this  to get it right but then they're not  overturning calls anymore and so I think  what they need to do is go to sort of  ask I judge I'm not a big hockey fan but  my hockey friends tell me that that's  kind of what they do in the NHL  whereas let's just play the game let's  not have unnecessary stops for instant  replay unless the sky judge sees  something that needs to be overturned  that's egregious that's clear and  obvious like the standard is that  they've set with instant replay but the  thing that fans hate more than anything  is being told one thing and then having  another thing don't spit in my face and  tell me it's raining NFL  if you look at what happened with Trey  flowers last night do you have any  problem as a former offensive lineman  you know Bakhtiari sold it a little bit  but flowers did not get his hand in his  face but they called it in those were  too costly penalties well I think what's  happened this year specifically is the  NFL really has sold out their officials  because they've said there's going to be  a renewed emphasis on Holdings on hands  to the face on the line plays whereas  those were the type of plays that really  the in the NFL they would let the  offense and defensive line play they're  not going to call ticky tack hands to  the face ticky tack Holdings but for  some reason they decided they wanted to  tighten that up in the offseason and so  that was a point of emphasis and so I  think whereas in years past  those were the type of calls that when  it's happening at full speed it's really  difficult to tell if that hand is in the  neck is it on the shoulder pad is it in  the facemask and kind of going into that  minutia is difficult at full speed now  as fans as viewers we have the ability  to go back and watch it frame by frame  and slowly see that that tray flowers  did not have his hands in Bakhtiari face  but what I think the NFL needs to do is  kind of go back to maybe the old  standard on some of these judgment calls  and say you know what let's let them  play especially in these critical  moments of the game it's too important  to not screw it up and it's too  important let's just let them play  unless it's really obvious in that  situation then you can throw the flag  but to be under the microscope the way  NFL refs are right now and then have the  NFL continue to push for kind of  splitting hairs on these judgment calls  in my opinion is a bad way to do it what  do you think the Browns need to do if  you said one thing that they must do  that if they're going to have a  successful season would be one well they  need to improve their consistency and  discipline and I think those things go  hand in hand early on in the season it  was a matter of penalties now it's  mental mistakes it's turnovers and I  think a lot of that goes back to  discipline I think Freddie kitchens did  a great job in his press conference  talking about hey this is the reality of  our situation in our team right now we  have a lot of talent but we're playing  as a group we're not playing as a team  we're not playing discipline we're not  paying attention to the details that  need to be paid attention to and so this  is their bye week hopefully they're  going to be able to go back and  maybe re-emphasize those little small  details because in football it's a game  of a million little things and you put  all those things together and that's why  the Patriots are good year and in you're  out they take care of every single one  of those details because no detail is  too important to spend time on but also  it's I want to simplify things when  things go wrong then you 